    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single `identityKey`-based check on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Core concept** \u2014 `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, computed identically for every owner. Two owners collide only when their **whole** keys are equal.\n\n**New files**\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 shared utility deriving the key from an `Owner` (or raw parts); telephone normalized to E.164, email lower-cased, null email/household \u2192 empty segment.\n- `RejectDuplicateIdentity.java` \u2014 the single consolidated check: computes the new owner's key and rejects a full-key match against existing owners with 409.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateIdentityHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2014 the 409 response.\n\n**Modified**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 removed `rejectDuplicateEmail/Telephone/Household`; inserted `rejectDuplicateIdentity` **after** `assignHousehold` (governed by the transaction) so the new owner's `householdId` is already assigned when its key is computed, and before `save` so it can't collide with itself.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` + `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the response, derived via `OwnerIdentity.key`.\n\n**Removed** \u2014 the three old `RejectDuplicate*` functions, their exceptions/handlers, and their escalation YAMLs.\n\n## Why this satisfies the spec\n- The single key drives all duplicate detection; the three separate checks are gone.\n- Because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different** telephones produce different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a 409.\n- Placing the check after `assignHousehold` means the key uses each owner's real stored `householdId`, keeping the comparison symmetric between the new and existing owners.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision` \u2014 second owner reusing the first's telephone, no email, no household \u2192 identical keys \u2192 409) passes.\n\nNote: the `AcceptanceBase` helper comment references a soft-delete on `DELETE /api/owners/{id}`, but `DeleteOwner` currently hard-deletes and there's no `deleted` flag on the model \u2014 outside this change's scope, but worth flagging if soft-delete-aware identity checks are later expected.",
